# BeeWare briefcase native-installer build artifacts. See
# docs/BUILDING_INSTALLERS.md. `build/` is the per-OS scaffold tree
# briefcase populates during `briefcase create`; `dist/` is where the
# packaged .msi / .pkg / AppImage land. `logs/` is briefcase's per-run
# log directory.
build/
dist/
logs/

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
docs/Session_Logs/
Docs/Session_Logs/*.log
Docs/Session_Logs/latest_closeout_summary.txt
docs/assets/*-reference/

# Agent process artifacts
# Ignore the .claude/ directory by default (local agent state, transcripts,
# caches, etc.), but explicitly track the committed rules / skills / agents /
# settings that codify the architecture (WS-T):
#   - .claude/rules/         agent-facing distillation of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
#   - .claude/skills/        repo-specific skills (code-review, etc.)
#   - .claude/agents/        repo-specific agent definitions
#   - .claude/settings.json  post-push code-review hook config
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/settings.json
docs-scratch/

# Dead-code audit scratch directory (vulture / ts-prune / AST scanner outputs).
# The architecture test ``tests/architecture/test_no_unreferenced_top_level_symbols.py``
# embeds the production AST scanner; this directory is just a workspace for
# rerunning surveys ad-hoc. See DEAD_CODE_AUDIT.md for the methodology.
_deadcode/
